<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $153.8 mln Sept 4.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $153.8 mln Sept 4.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $153.8 million surplus on September 4 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON SEPTEMBER 4</p>
<p>Exports: $212.6 million</p>
<p>Imports: $125.8 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $153.5 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $86.5 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $153.8 million</p>
<p>SEPTEMBER DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $703.4 million</p>
<p>Imports: $375.8 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $319.5 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $397 million</p>
<p>Net surplus: $250.1 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2324411</p>
